/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 456 0 R
/ActualText (- It is important to identify all interested parties that may rely upon or have inputs to your Quality Management System \(QMS\), and to understand their needs and expectations. This may include statutory or regulatory bodies, business insurers, professional trade bodies and others. It is not uncommon for a Board, shareholders and employees to be included, as they all have an interest in the quality posture of your organisation and how that ultimately contributes to success.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
