/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/ActualText (- Non-conformities can arise from different sources. For example, product inspections or measurements, activity monitoring, internal audit reports or customer feedback or complaints. All non-conformities should be documented as part of your QMS, and actions are undertaken to minimise their effect on your organisation, its products, systems and your customers. Prompt remedial actions should be identified and undertaken which are both effective and permanent, with the aim that the non-conformity should be prevented from happening again.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
