287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 558 0 R
/ActualText (Management review procedure and minutes of review meetings)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 558 0 R
/ActualText (- Your organisation's top-level management should undertake periodic assessments of your QMS, following an agreed procedure. This will allow them visibility of the component activities of your QMS, including data from activity monitoring, details of non conforming products, internal audit results, etc. Top level management will be able to act upon this information, perhaps focusing resources and support where it is most needed. The results \(minutes\) of management reviews need to be documented.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 559 0 R
/ActualText (10.3)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 560 0 R
/ActualText (Records of continual improvement activities)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 560 0 R
/ActualText (- There are many activities and supporting records which will provide evidence of continual improvement activities being implemented within your organisation. These may include audit findings, details of non-conforming products, customer complaints, data breaches or simply feedback from your personnel or interested parties, amongst others. The best practice is for the source of identified improvements to be recorded, which can then be supported by records of what is subsequently done to effectively implement improvement actions which address the underlying root causes.)
/Pg 19 0 R
